nosed intraoperatively by cholangiography and histological examination, and radicallytreated by left lobectomy, extrahepatic biliary tract resection and Roux-en-Y hepaticojejunostomy.Survival after operation was 13 months. Other similar cases reported in the literature are reviewed.</p>	</abstract></article-meta></front></article>